# api-services-utils

> **Purpose:** Keep backend code reusable, so routes and nodes never repeat logic.
>
> **Applies to:** `apps/api/src/**`

## Middleware (`src/middleware/`)
- One middleware per file: `validate`, `asyncHandler`, `errorHandler`, `rateLimit`, `runCap`.
- Every route reuses them. Never re-implement validation or error handling in a route.

## Services (`src/services/`)
- One service per domain: `runs`, `guides`, `reports`, `page-cache`.
- Services never touch `req` or `res`.
- Services take plain input and return plain output.

## Utils (`src/utils/`)
- Pure functions with no I/O: `normalizeText`, `hashUrl`, `withTimeout`, `slugify`, `sendSseEvent`.
- Every util has a unit test.
- Agent nodes reuse the same utils. Example: `normalizeText` powers quote matching.

## Clients (`src/lib/`)
- One instance each: Prisma, OpenAI, Tavily.
- Never create a client inside a function that runs per request.

## Config (`src/config.ts`)
- Read env variables through one Zod-validated config module.
- Fail at startup if a required variable is missing.
